# $1K Club -- Caddy reverse proxy config for the DigitalOcean Droplet.
# Installed natively on the Droplet (not run as a Docker container -- see
# DEPLOY_CLUB_DROPLET.md), copied to /etc/caddy/Caddyfile there.
#
# Deliberately does nothing beyond TLS + reverse proxy: the public
# route allow-list and fail-closed behavior already live in
# club-public-proxy.mjs (unchanged) -- duplicating any of that logic here
# would create two places that could drift out of sync. Caddy's only job
# is terminating HTTPS and forwarding everything to the one loopback port
# the Club container publishes.
#
# Caddy automatically requests and renews a real TLS certificate for
# whatever domain is listed below (via Let's Encrypt/ZeroSSL) the moment
# it can see the domain pointed at this server on port 80 -- no manual
# certbot/cron setup needed. Nothing here has been applied to DNS yet;
# this config only becomes live once club.scrollyseo.com's DNS record
# points at this Droplet's IP (a later, explicit step).
club.scrollyseo.com {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
}
